<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  THE PAGE COMING BACK, on a pop. subpage_enter.xml mirrored, and nothing else.

  It returns from where the push left it. subpage_push_exit.xml sent it to −16 when it
  was covered, so it comes back from −16 → 0 while the page on top of it leaves toward
  +16 (subpage_exit.xml): both travel RIGHT, together, and the close reads as the open
  reversed rather than as two windows arguing.

  Reusing subpage_enter here — which is what the app did — brought this page in from
  +16, the SAME edge the leaving page was heading for, so the two crossed. Read
  subpage_push_exit.xml for the full account; that file carries the owner's report.

  Timing and curve are subpage_enter.xml's, unchanged: @integer/motion_subpage_enter 260
  on @interpolator/ease_out_quint, because arriving settles. The direction is the only
  difference, which is the reason a second file exists at all instead of a parameter.

  API floor and reduced motion: identical to subpage_push_exit.xml — see the note there.
-->
<set xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:duration="@integer/motion_subpage_enter"
    android:fillAfter="false"
    android:interpolator="@interpolator/ease_out_quint"
    android:shareInterpolator="true">

    <translate
        android:fromXDelta="@dimen/space_16_reverse"
        android:toXDelta="0" />


</set>
